-- ============================================================================
-- DR9 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Perforation & Sand Control, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, so the seeded structure and the
-- shipped lesson files cannot disagree.
--
-- What this tier owns: the two questions the course asks and where they meet,
-- what a shaped charge leaves behind, the four dimensions a perforation is
-- reduced to, how a sieve analysis is read on the RETAINED convention, and the
-- two numbers that decide a completion type. It reads the two inputs. It
-- computes neither the skin nor the sanding onset, which are the tiers above.
--
-- THE READING THIS TIER IS BUILT ON, AND IT IS A CONVENTION. A grain size
-- curve can be quoted as percent RETAINED or percent PASSING, and the two are
-- complements. On the retained convention D10 is the COARSE end and comes out
-- LARGER than D50, which is the reverse of the intuition a passing curve
-- builds. Reading a retained curve as a passing one swaps the two percentiles,
-- and because the uniformity coefficient is a ratio of two of them, it ruins
-- that as well without ever producing a number that looks wrong. The check is
-- one comparison: on a retained curve D10 must exceed D50.
--
-- THE SECOND HABIT: every interpolation between two sieves is on a LOG scale.
-- A straight line between two points on linear axes sits ABOVE the curve, so a
-- linearly interpolated grain size is too COARSE, and a gravel pack sized from
-- it is too coarse with it. That is the unsafe direction, which is why the
-- rule is worth stating rather than assuming.
--
-- AND THE REFUSAL: where the sieve stack does not reach a percentile, the
-- engine returns nothing rather than extrapolating. A D90 read off a stack that
-- stops at 70 percent retained is an invention, and the tier teaches reading
-- the refusal rather than working around it.
--
-- The gun catalog here is a TEACHING FIXTURE. Its structure transfers to a
-- vendor data sheet and none of its numbers describe a gun anybody sells,
-- which the tier says in as many words because quoting it in a design document
-- is the error a course like this one creates.
-- ============================================================================

values ('perfsand', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-this-course-decides","title":"What This Course Decides","lesson_keys":["l01-two-questions-one-app","l02-the-hole-in-the-casing","l03-the-sand-that-comes-back","l04-what-this-engine-models"]},{"key":"m02-the-shot","title":"The Shot","lesson_keys":["l01-a-shaped-charge-in-one-paragraph","l02-entrance-hole-and-penetration","l03-shot-density","l04-phasing","l05-the-catalog-is-a-concrete-target"]},{"key":"m03-the-geometry-the-charge-leaves","title":"The Geometry the Charge Leaves","lesson_keys":["l01-four-lengths-and-nothing-else","l02-spacing-is-one-over-density","l03-the-effective-wellbore-radius","l04-the-crushed-zone","l05-what-the-geometry-refuses"]},{"key":"m04-the-sand-sample","title":"The Sand Sample","lesson_keys":["l01-a-sieve-analysis","l02-retained-not-passing","l03-d-values","l04-interpolating-on-a-log-scale","l05-when-the-curve-does-not-reach"]},{"key":"m05-uniformity-and-fines","title":"Uniformity and Fines","lesson_keys":["l01-the-uniformity-coefficient","l02-sorting","l03-the-forty-four-micron-cutoff","l04-two-numbers-that-decide-everything"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
